WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.860
Thermal comfort is crucial for human health and productivity.

2.1
00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:12.660
Corrected Effective Temperature is an improved index of thermal comfort.

3.1
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:20.660
Thermal comfort is affected by temperature, humidity, and other environmental factors.

4.1
00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:28.200
The body perceives heat through various mechanisms, including radiation and convection.

5.1
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:35.550
choice Aincludes sweat rate, which is not a factor in Corrected Effective Temperature.

6.1
00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:42.470
choice Bdoes not include air velocity, which is an important factor.

7.1
00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:49.990
choice Donly includes air velocity and humidity, missing mean radiant heat.

8.1
00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:57.080
The correct answer includes air velocity, humidity, and mean radiant heat.

9.1
00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:03.880
Corrected Effective Temperature is useful in designing comfortable workspaces.

10.1
00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:10.700
Remember CET as Comfort Enhanced by Temperature to recall its factors.

11.1
00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:16.850
Focus on understanding the concepts and applying them to scenarios.

12.1
00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:24.130
Refer to environmental physiology texts for more information on thermal comfort.

13.1
00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:32.010
Corrected Effective Temperature includes air velocity, humidity, and mean radiant heat.
